    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d523-a1">

                <pb facs="0619" n="535" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg535"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sifton to Mr.
                            Choate.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-07-02"><hi rendition="#italic">July 2,
                        1903</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: I have the honor, pursuant to
                    the treaty and the arrangement made with the United States agent, to deliver to
                    you 7 copies of the counter case of His Majesty in the matter of the Alaska
                    boundary, together with 7 copies of the Appendix to the same, Volumes I and
                    II.</p>
                <p>The additional extra 22 copies of the counter case and Volume I of the Appendix
                    will be delivered to-morrow, but as the notice has been so short, they must
                    necessarily be delivered unbound. I am sorry to say that we have no extra copies
                    of the Album (Appendix, Volume II) to deliver.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clifford Sifton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">His Majesty’s Agent before the Alaskan Boundary
                            Tribunal.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph H. Choate</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">etc.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
